# --- 2026-08-29: caches, vendored trees and eval anchors stay out ---
# 75 probe/sweep caches totalling ~1.0 GB; none was ever tracked. Several are
# well over GitHub's 100 MB file limit (l306_capture 276 MB, m79_knob_cloud 182 MB),
# so a blanket `git add -A` would have produced a push that cannot succeed.
*.pkl
*.pkl.*
# Vendored wheels / quarantine / pip scratch (~240 MB, never shipped; `vendor/`
# was additionally polluted by 262 .pyc, which is why stage() refuses to run).
vendor/
vendor_src/
_quarantine/
--no-deps/
bin_out/
_l136_linux/
_l136_final/
# Official-eval anchor JSONs (~373 MB). These are MEASUREMENTS, not source: the
# offline gates read them, and the long-standing convention in this tree is that
# they travel with the machine rather than the repo. Regenerate with
# iccad2026_evaluate.py / l117_linux_verify.py.
results_*.json
l*_ship*.json
l*_gate0*.json
l*_oos*.json
l*_linux*.json
*.prof
# Root-level probe output JSONs (per-case layout dumps, ~1.4 MB each). Same
# category as the anchors above: measurements. Subdirectories are NOT ignored,
# so beta_2026-08-16/ and beta_2026-08-23/ still go in -- the peer review's §C
# asked for exactly those.
/*.json
# Stray file from a shell redirect to the Windows NUL device; git cannot index it.
NUL
